   "text": "http : / / news . sky . com / story / 778356 / three - killed - in - athens - bank - fire - amid - strike Three <5 Killed> In Athens Bank <26 Fire> Amid <28 Strike> 7 : 00pm UK , Wednesday 05 May 2010 Three people have <6 died> after rioters in Greece <8 set fire> to a bank in Athens during a nationwide <10 strike> against huge spending <11 cuts> aimed at <12 rescuing> the country's economy . Greek police <13 clashed> with protesters in the capital as tens of thousands of people <14 joined> a 24 - hour <15 walkout> . The three bank workers - two women and a man - were <16 killed> when their branch <17 went up in flames> after a protester <18 threw> a petrol bomb inside . Firefighters <19 rescued> another five people from the balcony . Greek prime minister George Papandreou condemned the killings , saying : \"A demonstration is one thing and murder is quite another\" . He added : \"We will , of course , stand alongside the families who lost loved ones . This is the least we can do . \"To those who now mourn the loss of three children we say that the perpetrators will be identified and held accountable for what they've done . \" The general <21 strike> was <1 staged> as a <2 protest> against a new round of draconian austerity measures . Police <30 said> as many as 20 , 000 people <3 took to> the streets of Athens as <4 rallies> all around the country <23 kicked off> . Also in the capital , a large group of people <25 attempted> to <7 break through> a riot police cordon <9 guarding> the parliament building . The protesters <27 launched> rocks and petrol bombs at the officers , who <20 responded> with stun grenades and tear gas - filling Syntagma Square with chemical smoke . <29 Violence> was also <31 reported> in Thessaloniki , where a further 20 , 000 people <22 joined> the city's <24 demonstrations> . Greece has been paralysed by the strike and was effectively cut - off from the outside world . Flights to and from the country were grounded , while trains and ferries suspended their routes . Hospitals and schools were also hit . The Greek government is attempting to slice 30bn euros ( �25 . 7bn ) from its deficit over the next three years . The country has to save money as a condition of a 110bn - euro emergency rescue package from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund . Ordinary workers are furious . Trade unions say their members are having to pay for an economic crisis that has been created by corrupt politicians The vice president of the civil servants' union , Elias Vrettakos , told Sky News : \"The measures of the government overtake our historic gains and abolish our rights and return society back to the 1960s . \" Other union leaders have called the cuts \"savage attacks on workers' rights\" . Markets around the world remained sceptical about the bail - out , as concerns grew about the economic crisis in the eurozone and fears it will spead .",
